module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.CoherentModules
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.FinitePresentationFromCoherence

/-!
# The two notions of coherence on an algebraic stack, compared

Two predicates in this library are called "coherent" for a module on the big fppf site of an
algebraic stack `𝒳`, and the files around Stacks 103.17 are divided between them:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.IsCoherent` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.CoherentModules`, which carries `@[stacks 0GR6]`: the
  conjunction of conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks 0GR5, equivalently — on a locally Noetherian
  stack, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherent_iff_isCoherentModule` — condition (2) alone,
  finite presentation on the site in the sense of Stacks 03DL(7);
* `SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite`, the *sectionwise* condition of Stacks 03DL(8): the module
  is of finite type and, over every object and for every finite family of sections, the sheaf of
  relations among that family is of finite type on the slice site.

This file records the implication between them, and says what is known about the converse.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherentModule_of_isCoherentOnSite`: a module coherent in the
  sense of Stacks 03DL(8) satisfies condition (2) of Stacks 0GR5.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherent_of_isCoherentOnSite`: on a locally Noetherian algebraic
  stack a module coherent in the sense of Stacks 03DL(8) is coherent in the sense of
  Stacks 0GR6.

## The comparison, and the direction that fails

The implication Stacks 03DL(8) ⟹ Stacks 03DL(7) is a theorem over an arbitrary ringed site and
is proved in this library, at
`SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isCoherentOnSite`: coherence supplies, over each
member of a family covering the final object, finitely many generating sections whose sheaf of
relations is of finite type, and a finite family of generators of the relations completes the
generators to a finite global presentation.  Composing it with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherent_iff_isCoherentModule` gives the two statements below.  So
the sectionwise notion is **not weaker** than the notion Stacks 0GR6 defines; it is at least as
strong.

The converse implication is **not** a theorem over an arbitrary ringed site, so it cannot be
obtained the way this one is.  The structure sheaf of any ringed site is of finite presentation,
by `SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_unit`; a ring over which the structure sheaf fails
to be coherent in the sense of Stacks 03DL(8) therefore separates the two conditions, and such
rings exist — in `k[x, y_1, y_2, \ldots]/(x y_1, x y_2, \ldots)` the annihilator of `x` is the
ideal generated by all the `y_i` and is not finitely generated, so the sheaf of relations among
the single section `x` of the structure sheaf is not of finite type.  No such separating site is
constructed here, and no module anywhere in this development is shown to be of finite
presentation and not coherent in the sense of Stacks 03DL(8); what is asserted is only that the
converse is unavailable *by a general-site argument*.

On the big fppf site of a *locally Noetherian* algebraic stack the converse is expected, and it
is exactly the content the source extracts from conditions (3) and (4) of Stacks 0GR5 — a
coherent module in the sense of Stacks 0GR6 restricts, along a chart by a locally Noetherian
algebraic space, to a coherent module there, and coherence over a Noetherian base is the
sectionwise condition.  Of those equivalences this library has only the implication (2) ⟹ (1),
at `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isQuasicoherentFiniteTypeModule_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite`; see
the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.CoherenceConditions` for what conditions (3) and (4) still
need.  So the converse is open here, and the two predicates are *not* interchangeable: a result
proved for `SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite` hypotheses is a result about a possibly smaller
class of modules than Stacks 0GR6 names, and is not that tag's statement.

## Universes

`SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isCoherentOnSite` ties the universe of the module
sections to the universe of the coefficient rings, which for the big fppf site of an algebraic
stack is the universe `u` of its schemes.  Both statements below are therefore at module
universe `u`, which is the universe at which the Stacks 03DL(8) results of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.CoherentKernelCokernelLocallyNoetherian` are stated.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GR5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GR5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GR6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GR6)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u t

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Coherence in the sense of Stacks 03DL(8) implies condition (2) of Stacks 0GR5.**  A module
on the big fppf site of an algebraic stack that is coherent sectionwise is of finite presentation
on that site.

This is `SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isCoherentOnSite`, the implication
Stacks 03DL(8) ⟹ 03DL(7), read on the fppf site of `𝒳`.  No hypothesis on `𝒳` is needed. -/
theorem isCoherentModule_of_isCoherentOnSite (𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, t} B S hS)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p
      𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids B.topology le_rfl))
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite M) :
    IsCoherentModule B S hS 𝒳 M :=
  SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isCoherentOnSite M hM

/-- **Coherence in the sense of Stacks 03DL(8) implies coherence in the sense of Stacks 0GR6.**
On a locally Noetherian algebraic stack a module on the big fppf site that is coherent
sectionwise is coherent in the sense of Stacks 0GR6, that is, satisfies conditions (1) and (2)
of Stacks 0GR5.

The sectionwise condition gives condition (2) by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherentModule_of_isCoherentOnSite`, and condition (2) gives
condition (1) by `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCoherent_iff_isCoherentModule`.  The converse is not
available; see the module documentation. -/
theorem isCoherent_of_isCoherentOnSite (𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, t} B S hS)
    (h𝒳 : HasPropertyOnSomeSchemeAtlas B S hS
      (fun T : Scheme.{u} ↦ IsLocallyNoetherian T) 𝒳)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p
      𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids B.topology le_rfl))
    (hM : SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite M) :
    IsCoherent B S hS 𝒳 M :=
  (isCoherent_iff_isCoherentModule B S hS 𝒳 h𝒳 M).mpr
    (isCoherentModule_of_isCoherentOnSite B S hS 𝒳 M hM)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

end
